# The vim profile's `:term` takes the current window, as Neovim's
# `:terminal` does (NvChad: one window before and after, the terminal a
# listed buffer, `:b#` back to the file): a new tab in the focused leaf,
# the file's tab still on the strip beside it. `:b#` swaps back and forth.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
command view.toggle_tree
command editor.use_vim
ex term sleep 30
expect pane sleep 30
expect screen contains " 󰈙 a.txt 󰅖   󲀀 sleep 30 󰅖"
ex b#
expect pane a.txt
expect screen contains "alpha"
ex b#
expect pane sleep 30
# A bare `:term`: the login shell, in the same leaf again.
ex term
expect within 3000 screen contains "TERMINAL"
expect screen contains " 󰈙 a.txt 󰅖   󲀀 sleep 30 󰅖   󲀀"
